WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:04.069
It's just a wonderful, calm place.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.629
And you can grow things.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.309
There's a swamp right there.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.529
You can't drive anymore

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:10.969
past this road.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:11.839
This is a dead end.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.909
And I thought I would be left

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.319
alone here.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.729
This was the place where I felt the

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:17.689
most settled.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.059
And now I feel the most unsettled.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:22.899
Britta Serog and her family have

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.669
lived at the end of Burnet Road on

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.319
the outskirts of Syracuse, New York,

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:27.429
for decades.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.169
Serog's home and the surrounding

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.179
lands are now under threat, thanks

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:32.379
to a combination of federal

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.419
subsidies and eminent domain,

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.009
a legal concept that allows the

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.539
government to forcibly take

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.819
ownership of their land.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.919
Our property goes back to

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.509
that line of trees.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:45.549
Onondaga County has already acquired

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:47.199
at least 30 properties on Burnet

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:48.200
Road.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:49.809
Serog's neighbors were compensated

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.489
for their homes, but many sold

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.929
because they thought they had no

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:54.069
other choice.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.049
When we visited in early October,

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:57.789
Serog was one of the few remaining

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:58.959
holdouts on the street.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.869
For decades, Onondaga County has

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:03.489
been trying to develop White Pine

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.318
Commerce Park, which sits directly

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:07.119
adjacent to Serog's home.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.829
In the mid 2000, county officials

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.809
tried to lure an unnamed biotech

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.099
company to the spot.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.629
A decade later, it was supposed to

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.489
become a massive greenhouse.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.049
Now the county has finally struck a

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:17.709
deal.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.059
It's official.

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.039
Micron is coming to

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.474
central New York.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.809
In October, Micron Technology,

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:27.429
one of the world's leading producers

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.229
of computer chips, announced plans

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.759
for a chip production facility the

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.679
size of 40 football fields

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.969
with the promise of creating more

00:01:33.970 --> 00:01:36.489
than 9000 jobs in Onondaga County.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.599
Today's announcement

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.539
is the latest example of my economic

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:41.529
plan at work.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.269
The deal has been hailed by local,

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.129
state and federal politicians,

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:46.719
and some of the funding comes from a

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.219
federal bill championed by Senator

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.719
Chuck Schumer and signed by

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.699
President Joe Biden in August with

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.109
the goal of bringing manufacturing

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:54.249
jobs back to the U.S.

00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:55.289
from China.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:57.909
My watch, Made in America is just a

00:01:57.910 --> 00:01:58.839
just a slogan.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.729
It's a reality because of the

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:02.739
new law I signed and Chuck

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.869
designed and delivered.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.969
We're turning things way around.

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.619
Around in a very big way.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.839
Yes, folks, this

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.689
is our Erie Canal moment.

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.279
Schumer compared the Micron factory

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.749
to the Grand Public Works project

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.279
that in the 1820s connected the

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.199
Great Lakes to the Atlantic Ocean.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.819
That's what turned upstate New York

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.439
into an international manufacturing

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.039
hub.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.019
This is the largest

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.089
private investment in New York

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:28.929
history.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.179
We are gathered here as a result

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:33.039
of an exclusive, almost

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.629
never happening, extraordinary,

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.819
unprecedented collaboration

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:38.799
to be able to close on a deal which

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:40.659
would be known as the

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:43.269
investment of the century.

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.649
The head of the Onondaga County

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:46.299
Industrial Development Agency has

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:47.649
said that the semiconductor plant

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:49.869
will turn Syracuse into the next

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:51.399
Austin, Texas.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.019
Everyone in this community will

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.219
benefit everyone.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.669
Just before the holidays 2019,

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.879
they sent a letter in the mail that

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.929
they wanted to purchase our

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:02.889
property.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.719
Paul Richer is the co-owner of the

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.909
Hot House Brewery in nearby Cicerco,

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.649
New York, and one of the few

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.689
remaining residents of Burnet Road.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.949
My grandfather moved here on the

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.299
road in 1940.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.709
This is our home.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:16.869
My dad built it in 1954.

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:18.849
I was born in 58, so I've been on

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.559
this road my entire life.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:22.239
My wife's also lived on this road

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.619
her entire life as well.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.849
Her family's been here since 1850.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.089
We have two kids, two daughters,

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.229
two grandchildren.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.829
There was it was devastating.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.899
My heart really sank when

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:34.859
they wanted to come after our

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.090
property and our home.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.909
Eminent domain is typically used to

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:42.679
make way for public works projects

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.929
like roads, sewers and schools.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.279
But this isn't the first time that a

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:48.229
county or municipality has used this

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:50.029
process to transfer land from one

00:03:50.030 --> 00:03:51.979
private entity to another.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.809
In the mid 1990s, the city of

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:55.279
New London, Connecticut, used

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.869
eminent domain to take possession of

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.309
more than a dozen properties,

00:03:58.310 --> 00:03:59.899
including homes, businesses and

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:01.819
churches, so that the land could be

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:03.319
redeveloped into a Pfizer

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.489
Pharmaceuticals corporate

00:04:04.490 --> 00:04:06.499
headquarters and office park.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:08.419
The plan was to turn over an entire

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.919
neighborhood to a city economic

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:11.149
development corporation that would

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.709
then give it to Pfizer to build its

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:13.489
factory.

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:15.409
With, of course, promises of new

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:16.759
jobs and businesses that would

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.528
resurrect New London, another

00:04:18.529 --> 00:04:20.659
depressed former industrial town.

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.739
I won't leave.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:23.059
The battle between the city and the

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:24.649
community culminated in the Supreme

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:26.359
Court's Kelo versus New London

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.759
decision in 2005.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.589
Kelo is one of the most

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.449
reviled opinions that the

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.759
Supreme Court has ever handed down.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.079
Robert Belden is an attorney with

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.489
the Institute for Justice, a

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.019
libertarian legal nonprofit that

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.879
famously defended a property owner

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:42.889
named Susette Kelo from the same

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.606
threat that Britta Serog and Paul

00:04:44.607 --> 00:04:46.129
Richer now face.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:47.839
The legal battle over New London's

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:49.939
attempt to seize Kelo's little

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.799
pink house was later turned

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.569
into a feature film.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.579
The best course for us to improve

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:57.439
our city would be to acquire all the

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:58.440
homes.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:04.290
My God.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:06.039
Oh, my God.

00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.379
That was a 5 to 4 decision drafted

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.629
by Justice Stevens that basically

00:05:10.630 --> 00:05:12.519
says as long as a government

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.829
is creative enough to

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.659
come up with a public use or a

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:18.669
public purpose, it can take

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:20.589
a private person's property

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:22.269
and hand it over to another private

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:23.229
person.

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:24.699
In her dissenting opinion, then

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.529
Justice Sandra Day O'Connor warned

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.239
that the fallout from this decision

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.409
will not be random.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:30.969
The beneficiaries are likely to be

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.679
those citizens with disproportionate

00:05:32.680 --> 00:05:34.599
influence and power in the political

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.069
process, including large

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.199
corporations and development firms.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.209
A lot of people have sold because

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:41.409
because of the threat of eminent

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.029
domain, they don't you know, it's

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.919
really very difficult to

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.779
fight and they don't want to lose

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.999
their property to that.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:50.109
They feel they don't have any

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.489
choice.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.199
Throughout the process, Onondaga

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.879
County has insisted that eminent

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.009
domain will only be used as

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:58.509
a last resort.

00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:00.189
It's not a fair negotiation to our

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:02.169
clients when they are faced with

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:03.999
the threat of eminent domain if

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.679
they don't agree to sell their home

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:06.999
voluntarily.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.799
The oral argument for Kelo actually

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.269
talked about this, whether there

00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:12.189
were voluntary purchases

00:06:12.190 --> 00:06:13.719
by the city of New London, and it

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:15.819
drew a laugh from everybody

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.949
in the chain chamber when the

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.779
city's government said, Oh, a lot

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.459
of property owners have voluntarily

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:22.569
sold to the city.

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:24.429
I mean, everybody knows

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:26.259
that once you put this threat

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:28.059
out there, you're no longer

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.160
operating on an equal plane.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:32.249
Manufacturing employment has been

00:06:32.250 --> 00:06:33.599
steadily declining in upstate New

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:35.459
York since the 1960s, and the

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:37.019
Micron factory is one of thousands

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.429
of attempts, large and small, to

00:06:38.430 --> 00:06:39.749
revitalize the region with

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:40.919
government subsidies.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.439
A 2017 investigation by ProPublica,

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.909
Columbia University's Journalism

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:47.039
School and the Investigative Post

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.869
combed through 16,000

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.549
subsidy deals worth billions of

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.109
dollars handed out over the course

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.089
of four years under the oversight

00:06:54.090 --> 00:06:56.099
of former Governor Andrew Cuomo.

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:57.629
It found that the recipients were

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.549
poorly vetted, that the awards

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.589
yielded only modest results, and

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:02.789
that the process lacked

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:04.169
transparency.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:05.879
Yahoo was one of the biggest award

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:08.729
recipients getting $470 million

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:11.249
between 2009 and 2013

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:13.559
for a datacenter near Buffalo.

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.329
At the time, Senator Schumer said

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.069
that this opening says the high tech

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.359
companies throughout the world.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.189
See what stuff we have and you

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:21.599
will come here, too.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.279
In the years that followed, Yahoo!

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.079
Laid off thousands of employees.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.299
By 2015, the project had created 200

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.589
jobs at a cost of about $2.4

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.529
million each.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.599
By 2017, after having been valued

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.519
at over $100 billion,

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:37.529
Yahoo! Was bought by Verizon for

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.089
a fraction of that amount.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:41.339
And by 2018, one of the developers

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:43.319
in the Buffalo Project was in prison

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.759
for corruption connected to the

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:45.569
deal.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.669
Today, Senator Schumer is once again

00:07:47.670 --> 00:07:49.379
the driving force behind the Micron

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.009
deal.

00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:52.049
It's why I worked so long and so

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:54.509
hard and so persistently

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.759
for the last three years to author

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.009
and pass the Chips and Science

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:00.659
Bill. This project will

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.519
fundamentally transform the region

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:04.469
into a new global hub for innovation

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:06.059
and high tech jobs.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.619
Schumer's office did not respond to

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.509
Reason's requests for an interview.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:11.189
Folks, we're here to celebrate one

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:13.079
of the most significant investments

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.729
in American history.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.799
Again, not hyperbole.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.329
The county originally estimated that

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.889
development of the White Pine site

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.539
into a semiconductor factory would

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:23.129
create 4000 jobs.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:25.349
Now, Micron says it will create 9000

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.299
jobs, even if the company makes

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.379
good on that promise.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:30.659
New York's $5.5 billion

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.308
in economic incentives will work out

00:08:32.309 --> 00:08:34.529
to over $600,000

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.178
per job created.

00:08:36.179 --> 00:08:37.589
They throw a number out every time I

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:39.749
take when they hit a dark dartboard.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:40.619
That's where their number comes

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:41.459
from.

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:43.499
In my opinion, the state isn't

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.609
very business friendly.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:45.899
There's a lot of regulations in the

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:47.849
state and I don't find that

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.469
attractive to a big company.

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.269
I just feel that if a big company

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.099
does come in here, how long

00:08:53.100 --> 00:08:54.779
are they going to stay in?

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.639
When their benefits package

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:57.899
expires and they have to start

00:08:57.900 --> 00:08:59.579
paying taxes, are they going to stay

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:00.959
or are they going to move out of
state

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.849
like all the other big businesses

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:04.709
around here and companies have done

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:05.909
in the past?

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.129
And Micron's CEO has indicated

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.869
that the company will expect ongoing

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:11.339
financial support from the state of

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.379
New York to achieve its promised

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.579
job creation targets.

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:17.739
They're the biggest in the world.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.389
They're coming into Wisconsin with

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.549
an unbelievable plant

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:24.099
like we've never seen before.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:25.659
The Micron Project has a lot in

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.219
common with another eminent domain

00:09:27.220 --> 00:09:28.689
project that also relied on

00:09:28.690 --> 00:09:29.889
government subsidies.

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:31.959
A Foxconn factory on the outskirts

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.879
of Milwaukee, Wisconsin, that was

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.469
supposed to manufacture components

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:36.939
for Apple's iPhones.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:38.229
Then Governor Scott Walker gave

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:39.879
Foxconn one of the most lucrative

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:41.169
corporate welfare packages in

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.309
American history.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.989
Trump promised that it would be the

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:45.849
eighth wonder of the world.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.739
Developers bulldozed 75

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:49.899
homes to make way for the factory.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.459
When Reason covered the story in

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.469
2018, Kim and Jim Mahoney

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:55.389
were one of the only families left

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.069
within one and a half square miles,

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.299
fighting with the government to hold

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.409
on to their property.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:00.849
The Mahoney's, unlike their

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.739
neighbors, managed to stay put.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.769
Last year, Foxconn announced that it

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.359
was scaling down the project

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:08.949
significantly.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:10.659
Today, the Mahoney home overlooks an

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:12.399
unfinished construction site.

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.839
The residents of Burnet Road are

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:15.729
trying to avoid a similar fate.

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.679
The county raised

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:19.179
the specter of eminent domain in

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.009
August 2021, but

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.929
they don't actually initiate

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.669
the eminent domain process until

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:26.589
they send formal notice,

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:28.659
and they're really not obligated

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:30.489
to do that until they're ready to

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:32.679
do it. So what you have happened is

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:34.809
this sort of natural

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:36.189
I don't want to use prisoner's

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:37.839
dilemma, but sort of game theory

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:39.819
among the property owners in

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.019
this neighborhood.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.939
Do you want to be the last holdout

00:10:42.940 --> 00:10:44.799
who, you know, doesn't

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:46.239
get the price that your neighbors

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:47.919
got? You want to be the first person

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.809
to sell so that you can avoid

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:51.399
what has happened on Burnet Road

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.349
now, which is that the government

00:10:53.350 --> 00:10:54.759
takes some of the properties you

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.679
live nearby and lets them become

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:58.899
dilapidated and nuisances

00:10:58.900 --> 00:11:00.489
to the remaining properties.

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:02.409
It is certainly just sort of a

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:04.179
sword of Damocles almost hanging

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:05.679
over everybody's head.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.319
The county has forced people

00:11:08.320 --> 00:11:09.320
out of their house.

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:11.799
They didn't move by choice.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:13.329
They really had no intention of

00:11:13.330 --> 00:11:14.649
moving.

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.299
Everybody that was down here loved

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:17.169
it here.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:18.489
And they wanted this to be their

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:19.490
forever home.

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:22.599
A few weeks after we visited Paul,

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.249
he and his wife made the difficult

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.869
decision to accept an offer from the

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:26.870
county.

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:29.319
It's hard to duplicate what I have

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:31.209
here. We've looked around.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.049
Like I said, when we were

00:11:32.050 --> 00:11:33.339
negotiating with the county, we were

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:34.269
looking at properties.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.129
We were online wondering

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.869
where we can go, where we can find

00:11:37.870 --> 00:11:39.819
something that duplicates what we

00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:40.749
have here.

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:41.919
I won't say there's nothing out

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:42.969
there like this, but it's very

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:43.970
difficult to find.

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.239
I mean, just to have the same kind

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:47.799
of neighbors that watch out for each

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:49.509
other or friends.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:50.649
I mean, when there's a funeral on

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:52.329
the road, somebody dies on the road.

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.489
Everybody on the road is

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:55.569
at the funeral at the wake.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:57.999
Most of the homes on the street are

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.529
vacant. Some have been stripped of

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:00.549
their garage doors, lighting

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.649
fixtures, copper pipes and anything

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:04.509
else that the homeowners could sell.

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:06.609
Others have been raided by looters.

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:08.469
Serog has put up security cameras to

00:12:08.470 --> 00:12:10.419
deter crime, something she says she

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:11.829
didn't used to worry about.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.269
There was a real good community

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:14.270
here.

00:12:15.510 --> 00:12:17.249
Renee, still one of the people who

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:18.389
at the end of the road, she still

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:20.189
comes down here, walks her dog and

00:12:20.190 --> 00:12:21.869
starts crying.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.189
Even if the county succeeds in

00:12:23.190 --> 00:12:24.419
clearing out Burnet Road.

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:26.129
There's no guarantee that Biden,

00:12:26.130 --> 00:12:28.079
Schumer and Hochul grand vision

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.939
to return Syracuse to its former

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:32.009
glory or even to build

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.479
the manufacturing facility that

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.069
they're promising will become a

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:36.569
reality.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:38.459
After the 2005 Kelo decision,

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:39.899
Pfizer announced that it was pulling

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:41.909
out of the project in New London and

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:43.949
the land was left vacant.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.479
Earlier this year, the city finally

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:47.099
approved a new development to occupy

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.569
the spot where Susette Kelo and her

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.369
neighbors homes once stood,

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.229
consisting of a hotel and

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:54.989
ironically, new housing.

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:56.849
The Kelo decision sparked so much

00:12:56.850 --> 00:12:58.409
outrage that a majority of states

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:00.449
passed new laws to constrain the use

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:01.619
of eminent domain for private

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:02.639
purposes.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.679
New York State, however, did not.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:07.369
It's something we want to change,

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.699
you know, for everybody in New York,

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:10.139
not just for us.

00:13:10.140 --> 00:13:11.219
I mean, I've got kids, I've got

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:12.019
grandkids.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.169
There's something like this going to

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:14.879
happen to them down the road.

00:13:14.880 --> 00:13:16.889
And, you know, we hear about them

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:17.999
saying that they're going to take

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.889
our property kind of thing.

00:13:19.890 --> 00:13:20.939
They're threatening with them on the

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:21.749
mainland.

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:23.099
I just don't want them to go through

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:24.179
that stress that we're going

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:25.049
through.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:27.629
Our children and our grandchildren

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.609
will benefit from what we

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:31.889
announced today with jobs

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:33.749
and a future we could never

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.039
imagine.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.989
If I'm forced to move out, then, you

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:39.629
know, I don't think it's fair.

00:13:39.630 --> 00:13:41.729
It's, you know, taking somebody's

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.049
private land and giving it to

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.879
another private company.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:47.099
Is that the government's place?

00:13:47.100 --> 00:13:48.540
You know, I don't think so.

